        "id": "b70b5a22f3566644d767818020ea015fc287cab1",
        "tree_id": "d80df6cadb3f8245ac09ae282b0b0e6f96e7fa47",
        "message": "v1.0.80: atomic pairing + serialized translation queue\n\nRoot cause of '79 is still all English' (found in device log):\nThe translation itself SUCCEEDED every time (provider 'agnes' OK len=29,\nChinese rendered into tLbl), but three overlapping bugs killed it:\n\n1. Mismatched-pair guard had its comparison REVERSED.\n   Log: 'drop mismatched translation req=[C] cur=[A]' where req was the\n   CURRENT displayed sentence and cur was the sentence the translation\n   belonged to. Since ASR (4-5s/sentence) is faster than translation\n   (2-10s/sentence), the two could never be equal -> every translation\n   was discarded -> the box stayed English-only forever.\n\n2. Translation requests piled up. Three requests were in flight at once\n   (timestamps 804/809/813), competing for bandwidth; per-request latency\n   degraded from <1s to 10s, so results always arrived after the next\n   sentence had already replaced the English.\n\n3. Tencent Cloud was tried FIRST on every sentence and always failed with\n   FailedOperation.UserNotRegistered (service not activated), wasting a\n   full round-trip before falling through to agnes.\n\nFixes:\n- Atomic pairing: the overlay now renders English+Chinese as ONE unit\n  (showPending / showPair / showFailed). The screen is not touched until\n  a translation arrives, and when it does the English and Chinese always\n  belong to the same sentence. No more half-English/half-Chinese.\n- Serialized translation queue: only one request in flight at a time;\n  a newer sentence replaces the queued one. Keeps latency ~<1s and\n  guarantees callbacks arrive in ASR order.\n- Provider order changed to agnes -> mymemory -> tencent, and tencent is\n  disabled for the session after the 'service not opened' error.\n- SFSpeech partial results no longer trigger translation (they are\n  half-sentences that get replaced; translating them flooded the queue).\n- Thread-safe cache access (@synchronized) around all _cache reads/writes.\n- Hide the translation label when there is no translation, so a stale\n  Chinese line can never linger under a new English line.",
